On Fri, Feb 6, 2015 at 7:29 AM, Gleki Arxokuna <gleki.is.my.name@gmail.com>
wrote:

> How would you say "go to a meeting"?
> It implies not just going to a place but going to a place weith the goal
> to meet people at that place.
> Something like
> klama lo stuzi be lo nu penmi vau tezu'e ri
>
> But that's lengthy. Something more concise?
>

"klama lo te penmi"/"klama lo se jmaji"?

More generally, for brodas that don't involve a location place, you can use
"jai bu'u": "klama lo jai bu'u tigni" for "go to a performance".

I also don't have a problem with "klama lo nu broda".

mu'o mi'e xorxes

